6 0 obj
<< /Length 4142 >>
stream
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 738.0 Td (both at rest \(AES-256\) and in transit \(TLS 1.2 or higher\). Storage of Restricted data, including PCI) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 724.0 Td (cardholder data, is limited to approved, access-controlled, and segmented environments consistent) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 710.0 Td (with PCI DSS; primary account numbers must be rendered unreadable through tokenization or truncation) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 696.0 Td (wherever stored. Transmission of Confidential or Restricted information over untrusted networks) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 682.0 Td (requires approved encrypted channels, and such data must never be sent through unmanaged personal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 668.0 Td (email or consumer file-sharing services. Access to all classified data follows least-privilege and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 654.0 Td (need-to-know principles, with periodic access reviews performed by Data Owners and stewards.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 628.0 Td (5. Data Loss Prevention and Exfiltration Monitoring) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 605.0 Td (HPE deploys enterprise Data Loss Prevention \(DLP\) controls across endpoints, email, cloud services,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 591.0 Td (and network egress points to detect and prevent unauthorized movement of Confidential and Restricted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 577.0 Td (data. DLP policies are tuned to identify PII patterns, PCI cardholder data, and source-code) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 563.0 Td (fingerprints, blocking or quarantining prohibited transfers. Continuous exfiltration monitoring and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 549.0 Td (alerting feed the Security Operations Center, where anomalous transfers, mass downloads, and policy) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 535.0 Td (violations are investigated. Attempts to circumvent DLP or data-protection controls are treated as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 521.0 Td (serious security incidents.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 495.0 Td (6. Data Retention, Archival, and Lifecycle) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 472.0 Td (Information is managed across its full lifecycle - from creation through active use, archival, and) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 458.0 Td (eventual disposal. Data Owners, supported by Legal and Compliance, define retention schedules that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 444.0 Td (satisfy contractual, regulatory, and business requirements. PCI cardholder data is retained only as) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 430.0 Td (long as necessary for billing and legal obligations and is not stored beyond authorized limits.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 416.0 Td (Records that reach the end of their retention period are moved to secure archival storage where) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 402.0 Td (continued preservation is required, or scheduled for purging when no longer needed. Automated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 388.0 Td (purging routines enforce these schedules to prevent unnecessary accumulation of sensitive data.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 362.0 Td (7. Data Disposal, Destruction, and Shredding) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 339.0 Td (When data or the media holding it reaches end of life, it must be securely disposed of in a manner) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 325.0 Td (that renders recovery infeasible. Electronic media containing Confidential or Restricted data must) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 311.0 Td (be sanitized through cryptographic erasure or wiping to NIST SP 800-88 standards, and failed or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 297.0 Td (decommissioned drives must undergo physical destruction. Paper records containing PII or cardholder) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 283.0 Td (data must be cross-cut shredding or placed in secure destruction bins. All destruction of Restricted) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 269.0 Td (data must be documented with a certificate of destruction retained by the responsible custodian.) Tj ET
BT /F2 13 Tf 54 243.0 Td (8. Enforcement and Review) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 220.0 Td (Violations of this policy may result in disciplinary action up to termination and potential legal) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 206.0 Td (consequences. This policy is reviewed at least annually, and after significant regulatory or) Tj ET
BT /F1 10 Tf 54 192.0 Td (operational change, by the HPE Information Security and Privacy organizations.) Tj ET
endstream
